       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe limit for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2,000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** At 6 g/day, there is a real risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options for a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO every 8 hours (3 g/day).\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO every 6 hours (4 g/day, the maximum).\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours.\n\nTell me which one you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you meant 2000 mg/day or a different drug or dose, let me know. If you really do want the 2000 mg three-times-daily order, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. I'd recommend confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
